        "mocha": "^12.0.3"
      },
      "engines": {
        "comment": "Bounded to Node 22: the tests load xchain-vm, whose consensus runtime pins process.versions.modules to 127, so results taken on another Node ABI are not the fleet's. isolated-vm 6.2.0 ships prebuilt bindings for Node 22 (abi127) and Node 24 (abi137) alike, so the binding no longer sets the bound. See .nvmrc.",
        "node": ">=22.0.0 <23"
      }
    },
    "../xchain-vm": {
      "version": "0.27.0",
      "license": "AGPL-3.0-or-later",
      "dependencies": {
        "acorn": "8.16.0",
        "acorn-walk": "8.3.5",
        "astring": "1.9.0",
        "isolated-vm": "6.2.0",
        "mathjs": "15.2.0"
      },
      "bin": {
        "create-xchain-contract": "bin/create-xchain-contract.js",
        "xchain-foundry": "bin/xchain-foundry.js",
        "xchain-lint": "bin/lint.js"
      },
      "devDependencies": {
        "@stryker-mutator/core": "^9.6.1",
        "@stryker-mutator/mocha-runner": "^9.6.1",
        "c8": "^11.0.0",
        "eslint": "^9.0.0",
        "fast-check": "^4.6.0",
        "mocha": "^11.7.5"
      },
      "engines": {
        "comment": "Canonical runtime is Node 22 - matches the indexer's node:22-bookworm image and the V8 the validator fleet runs. isolated-vm 6.2.0 ships prebuilt bindings keyed by Node ABI (abi127 for Node 22, abi137 for Node 24; linux arm64/x64 in glibc and musl, darwin-arm64, win32-x64), so an install resolves a binding without a compiler and the dependency no longer sets the ceiling. The <23 bound is the CONSENSUS runtime: src/consensus-runtime.js pins process.versions.modules to 127 alongside v8/icu/unicode/cldr, so a validator on any other ABI fails checkConsensusRuntime() and cannot join the fleet. Widening the range is a coordinated fleet-engine event, not a dependency bump. See .nvmrc.",
        "node": ">=22.0.0 <23"
      }
    },
